// Tessera stdlib: F128 sinh, cosh, tanh
//
// Correctly rounded (to nearest, ties to even). CORE-MATH has no binary128 versions, so these run in three tiers:
//
// - quick: CORE-MATH's fast exp or expm1 path (F128Core/ExpShared.tess, F128Core/Expm1.tess) before its rounding,
//   combined in 128-bit fixed point (F128Frac.tess) and rounded unless the result lies too close to a rounding
//   midpoint for its proven error bound. About 1% of random arguments go on.
// - fast: the result in F128Extended (Standard/F128Math.tess) from e^a - 1 or e^a. It is kept when all of it
//   × (1 ± 2^-F128_HYPER_BAND) rounds to the same F128.
// - exact: otherwise the same formulas in F128Big (Standard/F128Big.tess, within about 2^-430 relative), rounded
//   once.
//
// The quick tier on a = |x| (2^-57 <= a below the cutoffs):
//
// - sinh, a < 1/2: m = e^a - 1 from the fast expm1 path, then (m + m / (m + 1)) / 2.
// - sinh, a >= 1/2: e = e^a from the fast exp path, then (e - 1 / e) / 2.
// - cosh: e = e^a from the fast exp path, then (e + 1 / e) / 2.
// - tanh, a < 1/4: m = e^2a - 1 from the fast expm1 path, then m / (m + 2).
// - tanh, a >= 1/4: e = e^2a from the fast exp path, then (e - 1) / (e + 1).
//
// Its bounds are proven from the error bounds CORE-MATH's own rounding tests rest on. The fast exp path's 2^x
// significand sig (leading bit at 123, so e^x = X × 2^(el - 123) with X in [2^123, 2^124)) is rounded there at
// bit 10 unless its low 11 bits lie in [1018, 1024], which is correct only when X - sig lies in [-1, 7). So sig + 3
// is within 4 units of X, a relative 2^-120.99 (cm_hyper_exp). The fast expm1 path below 1/2 (its result's
// leading bit at 127 or 126) is rounded unless its 15 or 14 guard bits lie within [-4, 2] of the midpoint, which
// is correct only when the exact value minus the result lies in [-3, 5): a relative 5 / 2^126 = 2^-123.68
// (cm_hyper_expm1). The fixed-point steps (F128Frac.tess) each lose under one unit, a relative 2^-127. In units of
// the result's last bit (2^128 relative units), with ε = 2^-120.99 and μ = 2^-123.68:
//
// - sinh below 1/2: m + 1 and the quotient lose 2^-127 each, so q = m / (m + 1) is within μ / (m + 1) + 2^-126
//   relative, and as q is at most half the sum the sum is within (μ + 2^-127) relative plus its own truncation:
//   2^128 μ + 2 + 1 = 23.01 units, so F128_SINH_NEAR_GATE = 24.
// - sinh from 1/2: e's error ε reaches e - 1/e as ε (e + 1/e) / (e - 1/e) = ε coth a, 1/e's floor adds 2^-127 of
//   1/e (at most 1.17 units, as 1/e < 0.59 (e - 1/e) from a = 1/2 on), and aligning and subtracting loses one unit of
//   e, at most 2 units after normalizing: 2^128 ε coth a + 3.17. With e in [2^k, 2^(k + 1)), coth a is at most
//   2.164, 5/3, 17/15, and 65/63 for k = 0, 1, 2, and 3 on, so the gates F128_SINH_FAR_GATES are 283, 219, 150,
//   and 137.
// - cosh: e's error reaches e + 1/e as ε tanh a, 1/e's floor adds at most 1 unit (1/e is at most half the sum), and
//   the sum's truncation one more: 2^128 ε tanh a + 2. With tanh a < min(1, 2^(k + 1)) for a in [2^k, 2^(k + 1)),
//   the gate is 4 + (129 >> max(0, -(k + 1))).
// - tanh below 1/4: m / (m + 2) carries m's error times 2 / (m + 2) <= 1, m + 2 and the quotient lose under a unit
//   each: 2^128 (μ + 2^-127) + 1 = 23.01 units, so F128_TANH_NEAR_GATE = 24.
// - tanh from 1/4: e - 1 is exact, e's error reaches (e - 1) / (e + 1) as ε 2e / (e² - 1), e + 1 and the quotient
//   lose under a unit each: 2^128 ε 2e / (e² - 1) + 3. With e = e^2a >= e^(1/2) in [2^k, 2^(k + 1)), 2e / (e² - 1)
//   is at most 1.919, 4/3, 8/15, and 16/63 for k = 0, 1, 2, and 3 on, so F128_TANH_FAR_GATES are 251, 176, 72,
//   and 36.
//
// Each gate is the bound rounded up, so the exact result lies on the rounded side of the midpoint (or in the same
// rounding cell at a binade's edge) whenever the guard bits sit farther from it than the gate (cm_frac_round). The
// arguments from CORE-MATH's overflow threshold of exp (about 11356.52) to F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW go on to the
// fast tier, beyond what exp's fast path is used for.
//
// The band is measured, not proven: on 20000 inputs per function (random magnitudes from 2^-57 to the cutoffs,
// plus both sides of the 1/2 and 1/4 switches, of 2^-57, 2^-56 and 2^-55, and of the cutoffs) the fast tier's worst
// relative error against mpmath was 2^-140.3 for sinh and cosh and 2^-140.9 for tanh, about the size of the first
// term wide_exp's series drops, so 2^-135 leaves about 5 bits. Results near a rounding boundary do occur: cosh x =
// 1 + x²/2 + x⁴/24 + … lies within 2^-220 of a midpoint for x near n 2^-56 with odd n, sinh(21 × 2^-54) and
// tanh(3 × 2^-56) within 2^-205 and 2^-220 of one, and tanh x just below F128_TANH_FLAT within 2^-200 of 1 - 2^-114.
// The fast tier alone rounds some of those the wrong way (tests/f128_hyperbolic.tess has them).
//
// Only zero gives an exact result. For a nonzero F128 x, which is rational, e^x is transcendental (Lindemann-
// Weierstrass), so sinh x = (e^x - e^-x) / 2, cosh x = (e^x + e^-x) / 2, and tanh x = (e^2x - 1) / (e^2x + 1) are
// too: each would otherwise make e^x a root of a polynomial with rational coefficients. No F128 and no midpoint
// between two F128 is transcendental, so no other input lands on either, and the tiers only have to be accurate
// enough to see which side of a midpoint the result lies on. Two ranges need no computing at all:
//
// - |x| < 2^-57: sinh x = x + x³/6 + … and tanh x = x - x³/3 + … are within x³/3 < half an ulp of x (the half
//   ulp below a power of two included), and 1 <= cosh x = 1 + x²/2 + … < 1 + 2^-115 rounds to 1.
// - large |x|: sinh and cosh round to infinity from F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW on, and tanh to ±1 from F128_TANH_FLAT
//   on (1 - tanh x < 2^-114, half the ulp below 1). Both are the first F128 past the boundary, found with mpmath.

module Standard::Core

/// The fast tier's error band, as a power of two: an F128Extended result is kept only when all of it × (1 ± 2^-135) rounds to the same F128.
/// :note: Measured, not proven: the worst fast-tier error seen against mpmath was about 2^-140.3, so the band leaves about 5 bits.
preset F128_HYPER_BAND: S64 = 135

/// 2^-57: below it sinh and tanh round to x and cosh to 1.
preset F128_HYPER_TINY: F128 = F128.from_bits(0x3FC60000000000000000000000000000)
/// About 11357.2166: the least F128 whose sinh and cosh round to infinity (the one below gives MAX - 830 ulps).
preset F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW: F128 = F128.from_bits(0x400C62E9BB80635D81D36125B64DA4A7)
/// About 39.8560: the least F128 whose tanh rounds to 1.
preset F128_TANH_FLAT: F128 = F128.from_bits(0x40043ED903114D00CEA0AEC526B52719)

/// The quick tier's gate for sinh below 1/2, in units of the result's last bit.
/// :note: Proven: the result is within 23.01 units (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_SINH_NEAR_GATE: U64 = 24

/// The quick tier's gates for sinh from 1/2, by k with e^a in [2^k, 2^(k + 1)) (3 for k >= 3).
/// :note: Proven: 2^128 × 2^-120.99 × coth a + 3.17 units, coth a bounded per k (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_SINH_FAR_GATES: @Array<U64, 4> <- { 283, 219, 150, 137 }

/// The quick tier's gate for tanh below 1/4, in units of the result's last bit.
/// :note: Proven: the result is within 23.01 units (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_TANH_NEAR_GATE: U64 = 24

/// The quick tier's gates for tanh from 1/4, by k with e^2a in [2^k, 2^(k + 1)) (3 for k >= 3).
/// :note: Proven: 2^128 × 2^-120.99 × 2e / (e² - 1) + 3 units, bounded per k (the derivation is at the top of this file).
preset F128_TANH_FAR_GATES: @Array<U64, 4> <- { 251, 176, 72, 36 }

/// The bits of 1/4: tanh's quick tier switches from expm1 to exp there.
preset F128_QUARTER_BITS: U128 = 0x3FFD0000000000000000000000000000

/// The bits of 1/2: sinh's quick tier switches from expm1 to exp there.
preset F128_HALF_BITS: U128 = 0x3FFE0000000000000000000000000000

/// Which hyperbolic function the shared tiers compute: `Sinh`, `Cosh` or `Tanh`.
choice HyperKind: U8
    Sinh
    Cosh
    Tanh

// -- quick tier: CORE-MATH's fast exp and expm1 -----------------------------------

/// e^x from CORE-MATH's fast exp path before its rounding, centered: sig + 3 is within 4 units of the exact
/// 2^x significand, a relative 2^-120.99.
/// :param u: The bits of a positive x with 2^-114 <= x below CORE-MATH's overflow threshold of exp.
/// :returns: e^x.
routine cm_hyper_exp(u: U128) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        fs  : CmExpWords3 = cm_exp_reduce(u)
        el  : S64         = fs.w2.to_wrap<S64>().shr(20)
        sig : U128        = cm_exp_fast(fs)
        // e^x = (sig + 3) × 2^(el - 123), sig's leading bit at 123
        r : CmFrac = cm_frac_normalize(sig.add(3), el.add(5))
        return(r)

/// e^x - 1 from CORE-MATH's fast expm1 path before its rounding: within 5 units of its last bit, a relative
/// 2^-123.68.
/// :param u: The bits of x with 2^-113.5 < x < 1/2.
/// :returns: e^x - 1.
routine cm_hyper_expm1(u: U128) -> CmFrac
    block entry()
        s  : CmExpm1Scaled = cm_expm1_small_fast(u)
        el : S64           = s.el.to_wrap<S64>()
        // e^x - 1 = sig × 2^(el - 127)
        r : CmFrac = cm_frac_normalize(s.sig, el.add(1))
        return(r)

/// The quick tier: sinh, cosh, or tanh of a = |x| from CORE-MATH's fast exp or expm1 path, rounded when its proven
/// error bound keeps it clear of a rounding midpoint (the derivation is at the top of this file).
/// :param a: The magnitude, 2^-57 <= a below the function's cutoff.
/// :param kind: The function.
/// :returns: The bits of the correctly rounded result.
/// :absent: When the result lies too close to a midpoint to decide here, or a is past exp's overflow threshold.
routine cm_hyper_quick(a: F128, kind: HyperKind) -> Option<U128>
    shared u   : U128   = a.bits()
    shared one : CmFrac = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 1 }

    block entry()
        beyond : Bool = u.ge(CM_EXP_E_OVERFLOW)
        branch beyond
            ? return(.Absent)
            : continue
        when kind
            HyperKind.Sinh -> sinh()
            HyperKind.Cosh -> cosh()
            HyperKind.Tanh -> tanh()

    // (m + m / (m + 1)) / 2 with m = e^a - 1 below 1/2
    block sinh()
        near : Bool = u.lt(F128_HALF_BITS)
        branch near
            ? continue
            : sinh_far()
        m : CmFrac       = cm_hyper_expm1(u)
        q : CmFrac       = cm_frac_div(m, cm_frac_add(one, m))
        s : CmFrac       = cm_frac_add(m, q)
        r : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(s.frac, s.exponent.sub(1), 0, F128_SINH_NEAR_GATE)
        return(r)

    // (e - 1 / e) / 2 with e = e^a
    block sinh_far()
        e    : CmFrac       = cm_hyper_exp(u)
        d    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_sub(e, cm_frac_div(one, e))
        k    : S64          = e.exponent.sub(1).min(3)
        gate : U64          = F128_SINH_FAR_GATES.getitem(k.to<USize>())
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(d.frac, d.exponent.sub(1), 0, gate)
        return(r)

    // (e + 1 / e) / 2 with e = e^a: e's error enters as tanh a < min(1, 2^(k + 1)) for a in [2^k, 2^(k + 1))
    block cosh()
        e    : CmFrac       = cm_hyper_exp(u)
        s    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_add(e, cm_frac_div(one, e))
        k    : S64          = f128_exponent(u).sub(16383)
        drop : S64          = 0.sub(k.add(1)).max(0)
        gate : U64          = 129.shr(drop.to<U64>()).add(4)
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(s.frac, s.exponent.sub(1), 0, gate)
        return(r)

    // m / (m + 2) with m = e^2a - 1 below 1/4
    block tanh()
        doubled : U128 = u.add(F128_IMPLICIT)  // 2a, exactly
        near    : Bool = u.lt(F128_QUARTER_BITS)
        branch near
            ? continue
            : tanh_far(doubled)
        m   : CmFrac       = cm_hyper_expm1(doubled)
        two : CmFrac       = CmFrac { frac: CM_FRAC_TOP, exponent: 2 }
        t   : CmFrac       = cm_frac_div(m, cm_frac_add(two, m))
        r   : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, F128_TANH_NEAR_GATE)
        return(r)

    // (e - 1) / (e + 1) with e = e^2a
    block tanh_far(doubled: U128)
        e    : CmFrac       = cm_hyper_exp(doubled)
        t    : CmFrac       = cm_frac_div(cm_frac_sub(e, one), cm_frac_add(e, one))
        k    : S64          = e.exponent.sub(1).min(3)
        gate : U64          = F128_TANH_FAR_GATES.getitem(k.to<USize>())
        r    : Option<U128> = cm_frac_round(t.frac, t.exponent, 0, gate)
        return(r)

// -- fast tier: F128Extended -----------------------------------------------------

/// sinh, cosh, or tanh of a = |x| (2^-57 <= a below the cutoffs) in F128Extended.
/// :param a: The magnitude of the argument.
/// :param kind: The function.
/// :returns: The result at 192 bits.
routine wide_hyper(a: F128, kind: HyperKind) -> F128Extended
    shared w : F128Extended = a.to<F128Extended>()

    block entry()
        when kind
            HyperKind.Sinh -> sinh()
            HyperKind.Cosh -> cosh()
            HyperKind.Tanh -> tanh()

    // (m + m / (m + 1)) / 2 with m = e^a - 1 below 1/2, else (e^a - e^-a) / 2
    block sinh()
        small : Bool = w.exponent.lt(-1)
        branch small
            ? sinh_small()
            : sinh_large()

    block sinh_small()
        m : F128Extended = wide_exp_m1(w)
        r : F128Extended = m.add(m.div(m.add(wide_one()))).ldexp(-1)
        return(r)

    block sinh_large()
        e : F128Extended = wide_exp(w)
        r : F128Extended = e.sub(wide_one().div(e)).ldexp(-1)
        return(r)

    // (e^a + e^-a) / 2
    block cosh()
        e : F128Extended = wide_exp(w)
        r : F128Extended = e.add(wide_one().div(e)).ldexp(-1)
        return(r)

    // m / (m + 2) with m = e^2a - 1
    block tanh()
        m : F128Extended = wide_exp_m1(w.ldexp(1))
        r : F128Extended = m.div(m.add(S64.to<F128Extended>(2)))
        return(r)

// -- exact tier: F128Big ---------------------------------------------------------

/// The same formulas in F128Big, rounded once: sinh a = (m + m / (m + 1)) / 2 with m = e^a - 1 throughout (no
/// cancellation anywhere), cosh a = (e^a + e^-a) / 2, tanh a = m / (m + 2) with m = e^2a - 1.
/// :param a: The magnitude of the argument.
/// :param kind: The function.
/// :returns: The correctly rounded result.
routine big_hyper(a: F128, kind: HyperKind) -> F128
    shared b : F128Big = a.to<F128Big>()

    block entry()
        when kind
            HyperKind.Sinh -> sinh()
            HyperKind.Cosh -> cosh()
            HyperKind.Tanh -> tanh()

    block sinh()
        m : F128Big = big_exp_m1(b)
        s : F128Big = m.add(m.div(m.add(big_one()))).ldexp(-1)
        return(s.to<F128>())

    block cosh()
        e : F128Big = big_exp(b)
        c : F128Big = e.add(e.recip()).ldexp(-1)
        return(c.to<F128>())

    block tanh()
        m : F128Big = big_exp_m1(b.ldexp(1))
        t : F128Big = m.div(m.add(S64.to<F128Big>(2)))
        return(t.to<F128>())

// -- the three tiers ---------------------------------------------------------------

/// sinh, cosh, or tanh of a = |x| between the cutoffs.
/// :param a: The magnitude of the argument.
/// :param kind: The function.
/// :param exact: True skips the quick and fast tiers (the tests use it to check the exact tier on its own).
/// :returns: The correctly rounded result.
routine f128_hyper_general(a: F128, kind: HyperKind, exact: Bool) -> F128
    block entry()
        branch exact
            ? slow()
            : quick()

    block quick()
        q : Option<U128> = cm_hyper_quick(a, kind)
        when q
            .Present(bits) -> return(f128_of(bits))
            .Absent        -> fast()

    block fast()
        w       : F128Extended = wide_hyper(a, kind)
        rounded : WideRounding = wide_round_within(w, F128_HYPER_BAND)
        branch rounded.ok
            ? return(rounded.value)
            : slow()

    block slow()
        r : F128 = big_hyper(a, kind)
        return(r)

// -- sinh, cosh, tanh --------------------------------------------------------------

/// sinh, correctly rounded: ±0 and ±inf give themselves, and NaN a quiet NaN.
/// :returns: sinh(`me`).
routine F128.sinh(me: Me) -> Me
    block entry()
        r : Me = f128_sinh(me, false)
        return(r)

/// cosh, correctly rounded: 1 at ±0, +inf at ±inf, and a quiet NaN for NaN.
/// :returns: cosh(`me`).
routine F128.cosh(me: Me) -> Me
    block entry()
        r : Me = f128_cosh(me, false)
        return(r)

/// tanh, correctly rounded: ±0 gives itself, ±inf gives ±1, and NaN a quiet NaN.
/// :returns: tanh(`me`).
routine F128.tanh(me: Me) -> Me
    block entry()
        r : Me = f128_tanh(me, false)
        return(r)

/// sinh x, correctly rounded (to nearest, ties to even), the body of {F128.sinh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True to skip the quick and fast tiers and compute in {F128Big} directly (the tests use it to check the exact tier on its own), or false for the normal three-tier path.
/// :returns: x itself below 2^-57 in magnitude, a signed infinity from {F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW} on, ±0 for ±0, and a quiet NaN for NaN.
routine f128_sinh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    shared bits : U128 = x.bits()
    shared nan  : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
    shared zero : Bool = f128_is_zero_bits(bits)
    shared a    : F128 = x.abs()

    block entry()
        tiny : Bool = a.lt(F128_HYPER_TINY)
        over : Bool = a.ge(F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW)  // infinities too
        when
            nan  -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            zero -> return(x)
            tiny -> return(x)
            over -> return(F128.INFINITY.copysign(x))
            else -> general()

    block general()
        r : F128 = f128_hyper_general(a, HyperKind.Sinh, exact).copysign(x)
        return(r)

/// cosh x, correctly rounded (to nearest, ties to even), the body of {F128.cosh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True to skip the quick and fast tiers and compute in {F128Big} directly (the tests use it to check the exact tier on its own), or false for the normal three-tier path.
/// :returns: 1 below 2^-57 in magnitude (zeros included), +inf from {F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW} on, and a quiet NaN for NaN.
routine f128_cosh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    shared bits : U128 = x.bits()
    shared nan  : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
    shared zero : Bool = f128_is_zero_bits(bits)
    shared a    : F128 = x.abs()

    block entry()
        tiny : Bool = a.lt(F128_HYPER_TINY)
        over : Bool = a.ge(F128_HYPER_OVERFLOW)  // infinities too
        one  : F128 = f128_of(F128_ONE)
        when
            nan  -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            zero -> return(one)
            tiny -> return(one)
            over -> return(F128.INFINITY)
            else -> general()

    block general()
        r : F128 = f128_hyper_general(a, HyperKind.Cosh, exact)
        return(r)

/// tanh x, correctly rounded (to nearest, ties to even), the body of {F128.tanh}.
/// :param x: The argument.
/// :param exact: True to skip the quick and fast tiers and compute in {F128Big} directly (the tests use it to check the exact tier on its own), or false for the normal three-tier path.
/// :returns: x itself below 2^-57 in magnitude, ±1 from {F128_TANH_FLAT} on (infinities included), ±0 for ±0, and a quiet NaN for NaN.
routine f128_tanh(x: F128, exact: Bool) -> F128
    shared bits : U128 = x.bits()
    shared nan  : Bool = f128_is_nan_bits(bits)
    shared zero : Bool = f128_is_zero_bits(bits)
    shared a    : F128 = x.abs()

    block entry()
        tiny : Bool = a.lt(F128_HYPER_TINY)
        flat : Bool = a.ge(F128_TANH_FLAT)  // infinities too
        when
            nan  -> return(f128_of(f128_quiet(bits)))
            zero -> return(x)
            tiny -> return(x)
            flat -> return(f128_of(F128_ONE).copysign(x))
            else -> general()

    block general()
        r : F128 = f128_hyper_general(a, HyperKind.Tanh, exact).copysign(x)
        return(r)
